    """
    The public address an entry-node enrollment is waiting on, so the operator can see what this end
    is dialling and correct it if it is wrong. Null for an ordinary enrollment.
    """
    entry_node_state: Annotated[str | None, Field(alias='entryNodeState')]
    """
    waiting | unreachable | notpasted | wrongsecret | collected. How the last attempt to reach that
    machine went, and the whole reason the bootstrap goes over HTTP rather than being left to
    WireGuard: each of these needs a different thing done about it, and WireGuard would have shown
    all of them as nothing happening.
    """
    entry_node_state_code: Annotated[str | None, Field(alias='entryNodeStateCode')]
    """
    i18n key with more about that state, when there is more to say
    """
    entry_node_state_params: Annotated[
        dict[str, Any] | None, Field(alias='entryNodeStateParams')
    ]
    """
    Substitutions for that key
    """
